f event structure.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_a60d6553\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"closure_wave\",\n  \"entities\": [18, 23, 26, 35, 42, 62, 64, 68, 80, 98, 102, 149, 270, 378, 1152, 1823],\n  \"window\": [22553, 34553],\n  \"confidence\": 0.78,\n  \"narrative\": \"Among the listed nodes only three triangles exist at all, one per node (step_04). Edge-time bracketing shows the closing interaction in each case trails its latest supporting interaction by roughly 2000-4000 time units, far beyond the 800-unit promptness criterion: 378-42 (~25k) -> 42-18 (~29k) -> 18-378 (>32.5k); 64-1152 (<26.5k) -> 1152-102 (~28k) -> 64-102 (>30.5k). The third triangle (23/270/1823) could not be resolved below the 800-unit threshold, but a single ambiguous triad is not a wave. Confounders were tested and rejected: the window has high volume and genuinely popular hubs with 163 static triangles (steps 02, 05), and the target nodes do form triangles once time is ignored (step_04), yet the repeat ratio of 0.0099 (step_01) indicates a sparse one-off structure with no rapid triadic closure cascade.\"\n  ,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_22\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_23\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_18\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_19\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_27\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_20\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_28\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_21\", \"role\": \"support\"},